# Laboratory — machine-local settings. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored (FR-J1: secrets never in repo/manifest/logs); THIS file is committed, so
# keep it placeholders-only. Anything already exported in your shell wins over these values, and
# a blank entry means "unset" — so leave placeholders you don't use empty rather than deleting
# them. Loaded by `lab.env.load_lab_env` at CLI/MCP startup.

# ─── Google Cloud (`--cloud gcp`) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GCP has no "API key" for provisioning — SkyPilot and `google.auth.default()` use Application
# Default Credentials. Pick ONE of the two paths:
#
#   (a) User login (interactive, nothing to put here):
#         gcloud auth login && gcloud auth application-default login
#         gcloud config set project <project-id>
#       Leave GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS blank; setting GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is still useful.
#
#   (b) Service-account key (non-interactive — what a `.env` is actually for):
#         Console → IAM & Admin → Service Accounts → create key (JSON).
#         Roles needed: Compute Admin + Service Account User.
#         Save the JSON OUTSIDE this repo, e.g. ~/.config/gcloud/lab-sa.json, then `chmod 600` it
#         and point the variable below at it. The path goes here; the key never does.
#         Also run: gcloud auth activate-service-account --key-file=<that path>
#         (SkyPilot shells out to gcloud for some GCP operations.)
#
# Absolute path preferred; a repo-relative path is resolved against the repo root. A non-existent
# path fails loudly at startup rather than deep inside provisioning.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=

# ─── Cloudflare R2 — durable artifacts (optional; `uv sync --extra r2`) ────────────────────────
# Enabled only when the endpoint is set. Credentials themselves belong in
# ~/.cloudflare/r2.credentials (AWS-format); do not paste keys here.
LAB_R2_ENDPOINT=
LAB_R2_BUCKET=lab-artifacts

# ─── Tunables (optional; defaults shown) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LAB_LAUNCH_RETRIES=3       # retries for transient local-API launch errors
# LAB_SUBMIT_STAGGER_S=1.5   # delay between remote sweep submits
# LAB_QUEUE_DIR=             # scheduler queue location override
# LAB_REPO_DIR=              # repo root override (scheduler host)

# Vast.ai (`--cloud vast`, the default) reads its key from ~/.config/vastai/vast_api_key —
# no entry needed here.
